From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(delegate): subagent.list and session.transcript give a subagent's whole goal and context

A viewer showed a subagent's task from its first transcript row, which the
viewer has to cut, and had no way to show the context the parent gave it:
the context lives only in the child's system prompt.

The child now keeps the goal and context it was given, whole: subagent.list
rows have context (and the goal, never cut), and session.transcript with
subagent_id returns goal and context. A running child answers from its
registry record, a finished one, or one read after a gateway restart, from
the goal and context stamped on its stored session beside its subagent id,
so they survive compression and a restart handoff (which rebuilds the child
from the goal and context it recorded). A child stored before this change has
no stamp and answers null.
